workedExamples.solution_text:
$240^{\circ}$ is in Q3, where secant is negative. Its reference angle is $240^{\circ}-180^{\circ}=60^{\circ}$.

$\begin{aligned}\sec240^{\circ}&=-\sec60^{\circ}\\&=-\frac{1}{\cos60^{\circ}}\\&=-2\end{aligned}$

$\frac{7\pi}{4}$ is in Q4, where cosecant is negative. Its reference angle is $2\pi-\frac{7\pi}{4}=\frac{\pi}{4}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (-2.3,0)--(2.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.3)--(0,2.3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw (0,0) circle (2);
\draw (0,0)--(1.4142,-1.4142);
\draw[dashed] (1.4142,-1.4142)--(1.4142,0);
\draw (1.2342,0)--(1.2342,-0.18)--(1.4142,-0.18);
\draw (0.7,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-45,radius=0.7];
\path (0.95,-0.48) node[inner sep=2pt] {$\displaystyle\frac{\pi}{4}$};
\path (2.05,-1.85) node {$\mathrm{Q4}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}\operatorname{cosec}\frac{7\pi}{4}&=-\operatorname{cosec}\frac{\pi}{4}\\&=-\frac{1}{\sin(\pi/4)}\\&=-\sqrt{2}\end{aligned}$
